ommit_sha":"7164a62e5bcc0a935563124fca5d0f532126c3cb","position":"1785904254299378001-519aebb3-8056-490a-bcff-e342163556f3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"84bb95bdb25a7ffe14723675351a2b9803f370c97a21dd28911c83c2b741df5a","event_uuid":"fb967d0d-52b5-42fc-88c8-01022e242329","position":{"commit_sha":"7164a62e5bcc0a935563124fca5d0f532126c3cb","position":"1785904255244945001-fb967d0d-52b5-42fc-88c8-01022e242329"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a0866ab12259b9ae58b2a72cc340d45d267ebee95b967635ed365880923378ff","event_uuid":"b500d82c-fbb8-4332-b38b-3231adf7d76d","position":{"commit_sha":"f00b23501f975bc42d8c8ddbbf9bf881e7bdcf28","position":"1785904290584167001-b500d82c-fbb8-4332-b38b-3231adf7d76d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-222_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"4cf58ecd-8513-4de1-a7b6-62b672e02919","comments":[],"created_at":1785903076714840001,"creation_channel":"python","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b500d82c-fbb8-4332-b38b-3231adf7d76d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6dfe-30ef-9403-477f"}],"description":"## Purpose\n\n`rebar metrics`'s structural metrics need three analyzers: **lizard** (Python, complexity),\n**scc** (Go, size) and **jscpd** (Node, duplication). They have reported `unavailable` in this\nrepository since they shipped, so rebar has never dogfooded its own code-health metrics.\n\nOperator request 2026-08-05: install them on this machine AND make new venvs in this project\nget them.\n\n## Corrected premise -- VERIFIED against the tree, replacing the original assumption\n\nThe ticket was written assuming *no bootstrap path installs lizard*. **That is false**, and the\ncorrection reshapes the whole ticket:\n\n- `pyproject.toml` `dev` extra self-references `nava-rebar[agents,metrics]`, and\n  `metrics = [\"lizard>=1.23\"]`. So `uv sync --locked --extra dev` and `pip install -e '.[dev]'`\n  **already** pull lizard transitively.\n- Proven empirically: a worktree provisioned by `make worktree` on **unmodified `main`** imports\n  `lizard` 1.23.0 successfully. AC \"a fresh venv can import lizard\" **already passes on `main`**.\n- `uv.lock` already pins lizard 1.23.0 (`uv.lock`, `name = \"lizard\"` / `1.23.0`), reached via the\n  `metrics` extra marker. So no lock update is needed and `uv lock --check` cannot drift.\n\nThe lizard half of this ticket is therefore **not a fix but a hardening**: the `dev` extra pulls\nmetrics *incidentally*, and its own comment says it is there so optional-capability tests RUN in\nCI. That is a CI-testing rationale, not a \"dev envs get the analyzers\" rationale -- so if that\nself-reference is ever trimmed, local venvs would silently lose lizard and `rebar metrics` would\nregress to `unavailable` with nothing to catch it. Naming the extra explicitly in the two\nbootstrap paths pins the intent independently of the CI rationale.\n\n## What this ticket changes\n\n1. `Makefile` `install`: `uv sync --locked --extra dev` -> `uv sync --locked --extra dev --extra\n   metrics`. Behaviour-preserving today (metrics already arrives via `dev`); the value is that\n   the dev bootstrap now states the dependency itself. Extend the existing uv-locked comment\n   (ticket ce5d) with this rationale -- do not overwrite it.\n2. `Makefile` `install-unlocked`: `pip install -e '.[dev]'` -> `'.[dev,metrics]'`, same rationale.\n   `make worktree` delegates to `make install`, so worktree venvs are covered by change 1 with no\n   separate edit -- confirm by reading the target, do not duplicate the change.\n3. Document the two NON-Python analyzers in `docs/local-dev-env.md`. They cannot come from a\n   Python extra, so a documented install step is the only route. Use exactly the commands proven\n   on this machine: `brew install scc` (Go) and `npm install -g jscpd` (Node). State plainly that\n   they are **optional** and that their absence degrades to a clean `Unavailable` in\n   `rebar metrics`, never a hard failure.\n\n## End state / scope boundary\n\nPost-change, a dev venv can run the **lizard-backed complexity** and **jscpd-backed duplication**\nmetrics. The **scc-backed size metrics still return a confident zero** -- blocked on sibling bug\n`c5b3-1b8a-08dd-40af` (the adapter omits `--by-file`). This ticket does not claim to make\n`rebar metrics` complete; it makes the toolchain installable and documented.\n\n## CI impact -- checked\n\nCI does **not** call `make install`. Every workflow invokes `uv sync --locked --extra ...` (or\n`pip install -e .`) directly, so no `Makefile` edit here can reach CI. CI also already receives\nlizard transitively via `dev`. CI is unaffected; no workflow change is needed.\n\n## Explicitly NOT in scope\n\n- Adding a `[code_health]` section to `rebar.toml` (scan_roots / size_cap). That is real\n  dogfooding config and must follow the scc bug being fixed, otherwise it would enshrine the\n  broken zero.\n- `code_health.enabled` is INERT (bug a573-00ea-2bf6-4eb1) -- do not set it expecting an effect.\n- Installing scc/jscpd automatically, or gating any target on their presence.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `Makefile` `install` names `--extra metrics` and `install-unlocked` names `.[dev,metrics]`,\n      with the existing uv-locked rationale comment preserved and extended, not replaced.\n- [ ] `make worktree` is confirmed by inspection to delegate to `make install` (no second edit).\n- [ ] A venv provisioned by the edited `make install` imports `lizard` 1.23.0.\n- [ ] `uv lock --check` passes on the change (no lock drift), proving the metrics extra was\n      already locked.\n- [ ] `docs/local-dev-env.md` documents `brew install scc` and `npm install -g jscpd`, marks both\n      optional, and states that absence degrades to `Unavailable` rather than failing.\n- [ ] PROVEN, not asserted: with `scc` and `jscpd` made unresolvable on `PATH`, `make install`,\n      `make lint`, `make typecheck` and the test suite all still succeed, and `rebar metrics`\n      reports `unavailable` for the affected lenses instead of erroring. Evidence recorded as a\n      ticket comment.\n- [ ] CI is unaffected -- confirmed by showing no workflow invokes `make install`.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"install and install-unlocked targets name the metrics extra explicitly"},{"path":"docs/local-dev-env.md","reason":"document optional scc and jscpd analyzer installs and their Unavailable degradation"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6dfe-30ef-9403-477f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"519aebb3-8056-490a-bcff-e342163556f3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"fd30-a088-cbbc-4dbd","ticket_type":"task","title":"Make the metrics analyzer toolchain explicit in dev bootstrap and document the non-Python analyzers (scc, jscpd)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4e32eb6d-178e-4815-aa61-add3752db0eb","9a0bd0be-4129-49e4-9515-4bccebc216e0","a3a417ab-234b-4f7e-bfd0-86d520c3d4e7","c8cf2683-1f23-40ce-9960-da6708b6ad79","519aebb3-8056-490a-bcff-e342163556f3","fb967d0d-52b5-42fc-88c8-01022e242329","b500d82c-fbb8-4332-b38b-3231adf7d76d"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785904290584167002,"uuid":"7b1a4688-2fd4-4a6a-8f20-bc43ff1d95ab"}